def X(id,n,c,isl,lon,lat,t,d,tip,approx=False,h=None):
    P.append(dict(id=id,n=n,c=c,isl=isl,lon=lon,lat=lat,t=t,d=d,tip=tip,approx=approx))
    if h: P[-1]['h']=h; P[-1]['x']='hist'
X('yasur','Mount Yasur volcano','vol','Tanna',169.4483,-19.5283,'Evening tour','One of the most accessible active volcanoes in the world. Tours drive to the ash plain and walk up to the crater rim, best at dusk when the eruptions glow.','How close you can go depends on the volcano alert level, so ask your tour operator or accommodation first.')
X('portres','Port Resolution','beach','Tanna',169.5035,-19.5248,'Half a day','A sheltered bay and village on the south-east coast, with black-sand beaches, yacht anchorage and simple guesthouses near the volcano.','Combine with Yasur: staying here puts you close to the crater.')
X('yakel','Yakel kastom village','culture','Tanna',169.4400,-19.5150,'Half a day','One of the best-known kastom villages in Vanuatu, where residents keep traditional dress, dance and customs. Visits are arranged with the community.','Pin position is approximate. Visit with a guide or your accommodation and ask about fees and photos.',True)
X('tannablue','Tanna Blue Hole','water','Tanna',169.22563,-19.43662,'1–2 hours','A natural swimming hole on the north-west of the island, listed in OpenStreetMap as a blue hole. Separate from the Blue Cave, which is reached by boat.','Pin position is approximate. Ask locally about access, tides and fees.',True)
X('champagne','Champagne Beach','beach','Espiritu Santo',167.11981,-15.14375,'Half a day','A famous white-sand beach on Santo\'s north-east coast, regularly named among the best beaches in the world. Clear shallow water and a calm bay.','Cruise ships can fill it; go early. A small entry fee is usual.')
X('luganville','Luganville','base','Espiritu Santo',167.1784,-15.5121,'Arrival','Santo\'s main town and gateway, with an airport, restaurants and dive shops. The base for Million Dollar Point, the Coolidge and the blue holes.','Domestic flights connect to Port Vila. Buses run in town.')
X('milliondollar','Million Dollar Point','sea','Espiritu Santo',167.2440,-15.5245,'Half a day','A snorkel and dive site where the US military dumped vehicles and equipment into the sea at the end of the Second World War.','Pin position is approximate. Go with a dive operator or ask in Luganville.',True)
X('coolidge','SS President Coolidge wreck','sea','Espiritu Santo',167.2380,-15.5330,'Full day','A huge Second World War troopship lost in 1942 after hitting mines, now one of the world\'s great accessible wreck dives, reached from the shore.','Pin position is approximate. Wreck diving needs a qualified operator.',True)
X('matevulu','Matevulu Blue Hole','water','Espiritu Santo',167.1746,-15.3774,'1–2 hours','A deep, clear freshwater swimming hole in the forest with rope swings and platforms. One of several blue holes on the east coast of Santo.','Take a snorkel, mask and sunscreen. Arrive early to avoid cruise crowds.')
X('nanda','Nanda Blue Hole','water','Espiritu Santo',167.1702,-15.3139,'1 hour','A quieter blue hole north of Matevulu, with turquoise water and a small canoe to paddle.','Entry fees vary; carry small cash.')
X('riri','Riri Blue Hole','water','Espiritu Santo',167.1812,-15.3909,'1 hour','A small, peaceful blue hole close to Matevulu, easy to combine into a blue-hole day.','Combine with Matevulu and Nanda.')
X('portolry','Port Olry','beach','Espiritu Santo',167.0706,-15.0425,'Half a day','A quiet village beach on Santo\'s north-east coast, with a calm bay, a few guesthouses and a base for Champagne Beach.','A good, slower alternative to town.')
X('tabwemasana','Mount Tabwemasana (Pic Santo)','vol','Espiritu Santo',166.75612,-15.36304,'2–3 days','The highest peak in Vanuatu, in the wild west of Santo. A guided multi-day trek through forest with village stays on the way.','Hire a local guide and arrange it well ahead. Expect rain.')
X('marum','Marum and Benbow volcanoes','vol','Ambrym',168.1364,-16.2494,'2–3 days','Ambrym, the Black Island, has two lava lakes and a huge caldera. A guided hike to the rim is one of the great volcano trips in the Pacific.','Hikes are arranged through guesthouses. Check volcano alert levels before you go.')
X('ranon','Ranon (Ambrym)','culture','Ambrym',168.1174,-16.1451,'Overnight','The north coast village and starting point for volcano hikes, with beach bungalows and the Rom dance and festivals.','Bungalow owners arrange tours; book ahead.')
X('landdive','Land diving (Naghol), Pangi','culture','Pentecost',168.1929,-15.9472,'Saturdays, April–June','The ritual that inspired bungee jumping. Men jump from a tall tower with liana vines tied to their ankles in the south of Pentecost.','Only held on Saturdays in the yam harvest season. Check dates and fees locally.')
X('lakatoro','Lakatoro & the Nambas','culture','Malekula',167.4185,-16.1068,'1–2 days','The administrative centre of Malekula, the base for visiting Big Nambas and Small Nambas communities, with a market and guesthouses.','There are no sealed roads. Guides help with village visits.')
X('southwestbay','South West Bay','culture','Malekula',167.4468,-16.4806,'1 day','A coastal base in the south-west for Small Nambas cultural visits and boat trips.','Pin position is approximate. Ask a local guide about visits.',True)
X('lamap','Lamap & Maskelyne Islands','culture','Malekula',167.8076,-16.4211,'1–2 days','The south-east gateway to the Maskelyne Islands, famous for the two-day canoe race and arts festival each July.','Pin position is approximate. Transport is by small boat and truck.',True)
X('lamenbay','Lamen Bay','sea','Epi',168.1677,-16.5922,'Half a day','A shallow bay on Epi that is known for dugongs and turtles you can snorkel near. Quiet beaches and basic bungalows.','Look from the water without chasing the animals.')
X('ambae','Ambae (Aoba) volcano','vol','Ambae',167.8379,-15.3713,'Check first','A large volcanic island with crater lakes, forest and traditional villages. Eruptions in 2017 and 2018 led to evacuation.','Check the current volcano alert and local access before planning a visit.',True)
X('lopevi','Lopevi volcano','vol','Lopevi',168.3453,-16.5103,'Boat or flight view','A near-perfect volcanic cone island that is best viewed from the sea or from a domestic flight between islands.','Active volcano: there is no landing. Look from a safe distance.',True)
X('sola','Sola & the Banks Islands','culture','Banks Islands',167.5497,-13.8748,'3+ days','Far north, the Banks Islands have remote villages, volcanic landscapes and the Rah snake dance, a rare traditional performance.','Reached by domestic flight to Sola. Allow slack for weather.')
X('gaua','Gaua (Santa Maria)','vol','Banks Islands',167.5108,-14.3065,'3+ days','A round volcanic island with a crater lake and active volcano in the Banks Islands, little visited and off the standard routes.','Pin position is the island centre. Ask guesthouses about guides.',True)
X('mystery','Mystery Island','beach','Aneityum',169.7747,-20.2486,'Half a day','A small uninhabited island off Aneityum, a favourite cruise-ship stop with white sand, clear water and snorkelling.','Cruise days are busiest. Ask Aneityum villagers about quieter days.',True)
X('anelghowhat','Anelghowhat Bay','culture','Aneityum',169.7914,-20.2273,'1 day','The main village and bay on Aneityum, the southernmost inhabited island, with a green, welcoming landscape and few visitors.','Reached by domestic flight and boat; allow extra days.')
X('erromango','Erromango','culture','Erromango',169.1331,-18.7672,'Several days','A large, rarely visited island with forest, rivers and historic mission sites.','Pin position is the island centre. Ask Air Vanuatu or local operators about access.',True)

X('tranquillity','Port Vila harbour wreck dives','sea','Efate',168.3133,-17.7375,'Half a day','Port Vila has more than 20 dive sites close to town, and operators collect divers from their hotels. The harbour wrecks include the Star of Russia, a three-masted ship from 1874 lying in about 33 metres of water with its hull intact. The pin marks the Tranquillity Dive base in OpenStreetMap, not the wrecks themselves.','Wrecks are for experienced divers; beginners have shallower reefs such as Hideaway Island.',True)
X('lelepa','Lelepa Island reefs','sea','Efate',168.2088,-17.5934,'Half a day','A small island off the north-west coast of Efate with reefs that are good for snorkelling, and the usual kayak and village-visit day trips. Pin is at the middle of the island.','Paddle or take a boat from the north-west coast; take your own snorkel gear.',True)
X('ngunapele','Nguna and Pele reefs','sea','Efate',168.3800,-17.4700,'Day trip','Two small islands off Efate\'s north coast, reached by boat from the Emua or Mangaliliu side. Their reefs are a quiet snorkelling option away from Port Vila. Pin sits in the channel between the islands.','Arrange the boat and a village host in advance.',True)
X('aorefan','Aore Channel fan garden','sea','Espiritu Santo',167.1900,-15.5450,'Half a day','Drift dives in the channel between Luganville and Aore Island pass sea fans on a vertical wall (the Fan Garden or Aore Wall) and a gentler reef at Cindy\'s Reef. Pin is in the middle of the channel, not on a surveyed site.','Dive with an operator from Luganville; currents make the timing important.',True)
X('tutuba','Tutuba Island reef','sea','Espiritu Santo',167.2764,-15.5662,'Half a day','A fringing reef off the south-east of Santo that dive operators use for relaxed coral dives and snorkelling. Pin is at the middle of the island.','Go with a Luganville operator who knows the best section for the tide.',True)
X('uripiv','Uripiv Island reef','sea','Malekula',167.4400,-16.0850,'Half a day','Just off Malekula\'s east coast, Uripiv\'s reef has been called one of Vanuatu\'s best and is a conservation area. Snorkel from the island with permission from the village. Pin position is approximate.','Ask the village first, and take a guide for the best section.',True)

X('sp_ww2_museum','South Pacific Second World War Museum','hist','Espiritu Santo',167.1732,-15.5156,'1–2 hours','A museum in Luganville about the Second World War in the South Pacific. Santo held the largest American base in the islands, code-named Base Button, started in 1942, with tens of thousands of servicemen passing through.','Pair it with Million Dollar Point and the Coolidge wreck for the full wartime story.',False,'WWII')
X('efate_ww2','Efate wartime museum and relics','hist','Efate',168.4125,-17.5366,'1 hour','Efate was also a major Allied base. OpenStreetMap shows a small museum of wartime relics on the north-east side, and an old landing strip a little further east. Pin position is approximate: OpenStreetMap places two museum points here about 600 metres apart.','Ask locally about opening times before you drive out.',True,'WWII')
X('havannah_ww2','Port Havannah war museum','hist','Efate',168.2598,-17.5687,'1 hour','A small Second World War museum near Havannah Harbour on the north-west coast, so it fits easily into a snorkel-and-lunch day there.','Combine with Havannah Harbour and check opening times first.',True,'WWII')
X('warmemorial','Port Vila war memorial','hist','Efate',168.3155,-17.7359,'15 minutes','The Australian and New Zealand war memorial in the middle of Port Vila, a quiet stop on the way between the market and the museum.','On foot from the central market.',False,'Memorial')
X('queiros','Queirós landing memorial','hist','Espiritu Santo',166.9396,-15.1652,'30 minutes','A memorial on Santo\'s north coast named for the Spanish explorer Pedro Fernandes de Queirós, who came to these islands in 1606. It is one of the earliest European contacts in Vanuatu.','Remote, so combine it with a day around Port Olry and Champagne Beach.',True,'1606')
X('missionhouse','Mission house ruins, Erakor','hist','Efate',168.3088,-17.7750,'30 minutes','Ruins on Erakor Island that OpenStreetMap tags as an archaeological site and names as a mission house. They are a reminder of the early church history on Efate.','Reached by the Erakor Island boat; ask staff to point out the ruins.',True,'Colonial era')
